`Promise.all` couples the two invocations: if `mem_stats` fails (e.g., transient open_db error in `panel.rs:266`), `setItems` never runs and the user sees a load error with a stale list. Stats is informational (banner + counts), not load-bearing for rendering — use `Promise.allSettled` or sequential `await`s so a stats failure doesn't block the list refresh.

```suggestion
      const [listRes, stRes] = await Promise.allSettled([
        invoke<MemItemView[]>("mem_list", {
          query: q || null,
          kind: kind === "all" ? null : kind,
        }),
        invoke<MemStats | null>("mem_stats"),
      ]);
      if (listRes.status === "fulfilled") {
        setItems(Array.isArray(listRes.value) ? listRes.value : []);
        setLoadError("");
      } else {
        setLoadError(formatCommandError(listRes.reason));
      }
      if (stRes.status === "fulfilled") {
        const st = stRes.value;
        if (st && typeof st === "object" && "total" in st) setStats(st);
      }
      // stats failure is silent — banner simply stays in last known state
